/**
 * #3934 (task 0 of #3721's model use-case plan) — every job a model does,
 * as data: the plan's §2 job tables, §3 presets and §5 locks, so the rail
 * never chooses its own three. GENERATED from the plan's comments on #3721
 * (6543041473, 6543052069, 6543057298, 6551079042, 6551512362) by the
 * scratch generator named in D1478's 2026-11-01 section; edit the plan, not
 * the rows, and regenerate.
 *
 * SHAPES
 *   USE_KINDS     §2's kinds, each with its full list in order. The plan's
 *                 lists are extended by every model a job of that kind names
 *                 (`extended`), so each job's Default is in its kind's list.
 *   JOBS          one row per job step: a job with several kinds (Retrieve →
 *                 Rank → Research) has one row per kind. Each row is
 *                 { id, step, kind, default, alternative, deeper, more,
 *                 fallback, presets, lock }. Deeper is §3's Best when it is
 *                 one of the row's alternatives and not already the
 *                 Alternative (the 3-model reconciliation); otherwise the row
 *                 shows two. A fixed row has no choices and no presets.
 *   MODEL_LOCKS   §5-A (c) tiers, with C (b): a partner model is on paid
 *                 plans only (nova-3 and Flux are always offered). §4 hides
 *                 glm-5.2 and the 3.1 70B.
 *   LEGAL_HOLD    D (a): until Legal reads each vendor's terms, no rail lists
 *                 these. The read gates offering them, not the code.
 *   COVERAGE      §1's set: 60 offered, 14 not offered, plus the two rows the
 *                 catalogue gained after the plan (clairic, beta; v4.1 flash,
 *                 held for the owner's spend approval, B (c)).
 *   RAIL_KIND_JOBS  the job step each canvas kind's page row reads.
 *   DECK_ELEMENT_JOBS  a job id per `deckV2Model.js` element group and item.
 */

